{"text": "ASSOCIATES, LLC\nMANAGEMENT ADVISORS\n\nQE SHAEVSKY\n\nVia Email September 4, 2020\n\nHonorable Dana Nessel\nOffice of the Attorney General\nG. Mennen Williams Bldg.\n525 W. Ottawa Street\nP.O. Box 30212\n\nLansing, MI 48909\n\nDear Attorney General Nessel,\n\nRe: Beaumont Health\n\n| am writing this letter to you as a strong supporter of Beaumont Health and as a concerned citizen to\nask you to intervene in the governing of Beaumont Health within your duty and responsibility to oversee\nand protect the charitable interests within the State of Michigan.\n\nBy way of introduction, by profession | am a lawyer and was a senior partner for many years ina\nprominent Michigan law firm. | am currently a business advisor to small and medium-sized businesses\nand to several families. For approximately 17 years (ending in 2014), | was a Director (or Trustee) of\nBeaumont. As a Director, | was, at various times, Vice Chair of the Board, Chair of the Finance\nCommittee, Chair of the Audit Committee, and a member of the Investment Committee. | have been a\npatient of, and donor to, Beaumont, and three of my grandchildren were born at Beaumont. So, |ama\nstrong supporter of Beaumont Health\u2014and that is why | find it necessary to urge you to take certain\nactions to protect the long term viability of Beaumont Health and the health and wellness of the people\nof the State of Michigan served by Beaumont Health, the largest hospital and health care providing\nsystem in Michigan.\n\nIt is not hyperbole to say that there are two life and death issues currently facing Beaumont Health\nthat require your intervention and should be addressed by your Office as part of your inherent\nresponsibility to ensure that non-profit organizations in Michigan are carrying out their missions. The\nfirst is the proposed transaction to turn over control of Beaumont Health to AdvocateAuroraHealth,\nheadquartered in Chicago. The second is that Beaumont Health operations have become dysfunctional,\nas reflected in complete discord between top administrative executives and Beaumont professionals\n(physicians, nurses and staff) where the professionals have lost all confidence in management's actions,\nresulting in the jeopardizing of patient health and safety.\n\nKEKKKEKKAKKKKKAKEKKKKKKEKEREREAKAK\n\n2 esa SSS SESS SESE SSS SSE SSS SS SSSR SE ES ESSE\n30833 Northwestern Hwy., Suite 200 | Farmington Hills, Michigan 48334\n248.737.0808 (p) | 248.737.8811 (f)",
